Instead of maintaining a custom recursive `cloneJsonValue` utility, we can leverage the native, standard `structuredClone` function. This reduces code duplication, improves performance, and handles complex nested structures more robustly.

```javascript
function cloneJsonValue(value) {
  return structuredClone(value);
}
